@startuml UC-A7-sign-in-through-company-single-sign-on-design-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
title UC-A7 Sign in through company SSO (design sequence, planned)
' Design level (decision 9). The analysis level is UC-A7-sign-in-through-company-single-sign-on-analysis-sequence.puml.
' Step ids are the main flow numbers of UC-A7. Release 2: not built. Steps 1 and 5 are UC-A1.
' Evolved from MK3 UC-A6: a realm setting, with no change to our code.

actor "Person" as P
participant "Web server" as W #E6F0FB
participant "Keycloak" as K #ECECEC
participant "Company\nlogin" as C #ECECEC
participant "API" as A #E6F0FB

P -> W : 1 sign in (as UC-A1)
W --> P : 1 redirect to Keycloak
P -> K : 2 choose the company login
K --> P : 3 redirect to the company login
P -> C : 3 sign in there
alt company login refuses
  C --> K : error
  K --> P : error page, no token
else
  C --> K : 4 signed answer
  K -> K : 4 create or find the Keycloak user
  K --> P : 5 back with code
  P -> W : 5 callback, session made (UC-A1)
  W -> A : 6 first request + access token
  A -> A : 6 pending account if none (UC-A3)
end
@enduml
